@H2 6.6 Delivery means: above land, below land, maintenance, other
@P Options for power, water and data were scored on 9 criteria (capex, wind, flood, fire, seismic, repair speed, inspectability, adaptability, safety). Safety is a hard constraint: options scoring below 3 are excluded. Weights follow the hazard profile; stability = share of 1000 random perturbations (+-50% weights, +-1 score) in which each option wins. Result for the reference site: POWER = {{res.means.current.power.best}}, WATER = {{res.means.current.water.best}}, DATA = {{res.means.current.data.best}}.
{{table:means}}
@P ABOVE LAND (overhead lines) loses on wind, fire and safety in every profile; it remains only as temporary restoration (surface_temporary). BELOW LAND buried direct is robust but slow to repair and impossible to inspect. UTILITY GALLERIES score best on maintenance but cost most and flood badly. The ACCESSIBLE TROUGH (dry, LV) plus LIFTABLE WET STRIP gives below-land protection with above-land maintainability. OTHER: in-structure routing through colonnade columns, wireless mesh for data, and hilltop reservoirs as gravity buffers.
@H2 6.7 Interaction engine and co-location benefits
@P 23 subsystems are encoded with zones, outputs, inputs and data links (efe_city/synergy.py). Pairs are classed automatically; extend the table to add a subsystem and the matrix, counts and conflicts update.
